    { id: "q-er4-input", category: "er", prompt: "Cambridge IGCSE 0478/21, May/June 2024, Question 4\nThis pseudocode algorithm is intended to allow 10 values to be entered and totalled. The total of the entered values is output at the end of the algorithm.\n01 DECLARE Loop : STRING\n02 DECLARE Value : REAL\n03 DECLARE Total : REAL\n04 Total ← 0\n05 IF Loop ← 1 TO 10\n06     OUTPUT \"Enter a number\"\n07     INPUT Loop\n08     Total ← Total * Value\n09 NEXT Loop\n10 OUTPUT \"The total of the numbers entered is \", Total\nLine 07 has one of the errors. Suggest a correction: write the correct line.", answers: ["INPUT Value"], keywords: [/^\s*(INPUT\s*Value)\s*\.?\s*$/i], distractors: ["INPUT Total", "OUTPUT Value", "INPUT Loop"], working: ["Which variable is added to Total on the next line?", "So which variable must get the number the user types?"], note: "Line 01: Loop counts 1 to 10, so it must be an INTEGER, not a STRING.\nLine 05: a loop that repeats 10 times is a FOR loop, not IF: FOR Loop ← 1 TO 10.\nLine 07: the number typed must go into Value, so INPUT Value.\nLine 08: the total must add each value, so Total ← Total + Value.\nAnswer: 01 INTEGER, 05 FOR, 07 INPUT Value, 08 Total ← Total + Value" },
    { id: "q-er4-add", category: "er", prompt: "Cambridge IGCSE 0478/21, May/June 2024, Question 4\nThis pseudocode algorithm is intended to allow 10 values to be entered and totalled. The total of the entered values is output at the end of the algorithm.\n01 DECLARE Loop : STRING\n02 DECLARE Value : REAL\n03 DECLARE Total : REAL\n04 Total ← 0\n05 IF Loop ← 1 TO 10\n06     OUTPUT \"Enter a number\"\n07     INPUT Loop\n08     Total ← Total * Value\n09 NEXT Loop\n10 OUTPUT \"The total of the numbers entered is \", Total\nLine 08 has one of the errors. Suggest a correction: write the correct line.", answers: ["Total ← Total + Value"], keywords: [/^\s*(Total\s*(←|<-|<--|=)\s*Total\s*\+\s*Value|Total\s*(←|<-|<--|=)\s*Value\s*\+\s*Total)\s*\.?\s*$/i], distractors: ["Total ← Total * Value", "Total ← Value", "Total ← Total + Loop"], working: ["Total starts at 0. What happens to 0 when you multiply it?", "A total adds each new value to the old total."], note: "Line 01: Loop counts 1 to 10, so it must be an INTEGER, not a STRING.\nLine 05: a loop that repeats 10 times is a FOR loop, not IF: FOR Loop ← 1 TO 10.\nLine 07: the number typed must go into Value, so INPUT Value.\nLine 08: the total must add each value, so Total ← Total + Value.\nAnswer: 01 INTEGER, 05 FOR, 07 INPUT Value, 08 Total ← Total + Value" },
    { id: "q-ex-purpose", category: "ex", prompt: "A student is given a program that has an error.\nExplain why the student should know the purpose of the program before looking for the error.", answers: ["The purpose says what it should output, so you can compare it with what a trace shows it really does"], keywords: [/^(?=.*\b(output|outputs|do|does|job|result|results)\b)(?=.*\b(should|supposed|meant|intended|expected)\b)(?=.*\b(compare|compared|comparing|different|difference|match|matches|trace|traced|tracing|actually|really)\b)/i], distractors: ["The purpose shows which line number has the error in the program", "Knowing the purpose makes the program run faster when it is traced", "The purpose lists every variable, so you can check each DECLARE line"], working: ["A program can run with no error message and still do the wrong job. How would you notice?", "You need two things to compare: what it should do, and what it really does."], note: "A program can run with no error message and still do the wrong job.\nThe purpose tells you what it should output.\nA trace shows what it really does, so you compare the two and find where they are different.\nAnswer: the purpose says what it should output, so you can compare it with what a trace shows it really does" }
